{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"ssr-and-client-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and Client Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The recommended architecture is hydrated SSR: highlight the initial document on the server, then reuse the same synchronous registry for client navigations and dynamic content."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"isomorphic-module","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Isomorphic module"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/lib/highlight.ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\nimport { shell } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/shell'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\n\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, json, shell, ts, tsx],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not put server-only imports in this module. The highlighter itself needs none."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-path","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server path"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Highlight before serializing or streaming the code block:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const data = highlighter.renderCodeBlockData({\n  code,\n  lang,\n  title,\n  decorations,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send or render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.htmlMarkup"},{"type":"text","value":". Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.copyText"},{"type":"text","value":" for a copy button."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-rendered code does not need to be highlighted again. It is already static HTML controlled by CSS."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the client highlighter only for code introduced after hydration:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side route content not included in the initial payload"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Markdown previews"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactive examples that change source"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User-selected language variants"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"determinism","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Determinism"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server and client output match when all of these match:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source string"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language registrations and order"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language option"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decorations and line-number option"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package version"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Themes do not affect highlighted markup."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"avoid-hydration-mismatches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avoid hydration mismatches"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Export one registry module used by both paths."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not conditionally register languages with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window"},{"type":"text","value":" checks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normalize Markdown fence metadata before rendering on both paths."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not highlight trimmed code on one path and untrimmed code on the other."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderCodeBlockData()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderCodeFence()"},{"type":"text","value":" trim trailing block whitespace consistently for copy/render workflows. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlight()"},{"type":"text","value":" preserves its input exactly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"caching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caching"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The highlighter is fast enough for normal docs pages without a cache. For large static builds, cache by package version, language, source, and decoration options if build time becomes material."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not cache theme variants separately. They share the same HTML."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-no-worker","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why no worker?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The docs-sized path is synchronous and usually much cheaper than worker startup and message serialization. A worker is reasonable only for unusually large interactive inputs, which is outside the primary use case."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"ssr-and-client-rendering","text":"SSR and Client Rendering","level":1},{"id":"isomorphic-module","text":"Isomorphic module","level":2},{"id":"server-path","text":"Server path","level":2},{"id":"hydration","text":"Hydration","level":2},{"id":"determinism","text":"Determinism","level":2},{"id":"avoid-hydration-mismatches","text":"Avoid hydration mismatches","level":2},{"id":"caching","text":"Caching","level":2},{"id":"why-no-worker","text":"Why no worker?","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# SSR and Client Rendering\n\nThe recommended architecture is hydrated SSR: highlight the initial document on the server, then reuse the same synchronous registry for client navigations and dynamic content.\n\n## Isomorphic module\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/highlight.ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\nimport { shell } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/shell'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\n\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, json, shell, ts, tsx],\n})\n```\n\nDo not put server-only imports in this module. The highlighter itself needs none.\n\n## Server path\n\nHighlight before serializing or streaming the code block:\n\n```ts\nconst data = highlighter.renderCodeBlockData({\n  code,\n  lang,\n  title,\n  decorations,\n})\n```\n\nSend or render `data.htmlMarkup`. Keep `data.copyText` for a copy button.\n\n## Hydration\n\nServer-rendered code does not need to be highlighted again. It is already static HTML controlled by CSS.\n\nUse the client highlighter only for code introduced after hydration:\n\n- Client-side route content not included in the initial payload\n- Live Markdown previews\n- Interactive examples that change source\n- User-selected language variants\n\n## Determinism\n\nServer and client output match when all of these match:\n\n- Source string\n- Language registrations and order\n- Language option\n- Decorations and line-number option\n- Package version\n\nThemes do not affect highlighted markup.\n\n## Avoid hydration mismatches\n\n- Export one registry module used by both paths.\n- Do not conditionally register languages with `window` checks.\n- Normalize Markdown fence metadata before rendering on both paths.\n- Do not highlight trimmed code on one path and untrimmed code on the other.\n\n`renderCodeBlockData()` and `renderCodeFence()` trim trailing block whitespace consistently for copy/render workflows. `highlight()` preserves its input exactly.\n\n## Caching\n\nThe highlighter is fast enough for normal docs pages without a cache. For large static builds, cache by package version, language, source, and decoration options if build time becomes material.\n\nDo not cache theme variants separately. They share the same HTML.\n\n## Why no worker?\n\nThe docs-sized path is synchronous and usually much cheaper than worker startup and message serialization. A worker is reasonable only for unusually large interactive inputs, which is outside the primary use case.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: SSR and Client Rendering\n---\n\n# SSR and Client Rendering\n\nThe recommended architecture is hydrated SSR: highlight the initial document on the server, then reuse the same synchronous registry for client navigations and dynamic content.\n\n## Isomorphic module\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/highlight.ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\nimport { shell } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/shell'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\n\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, json, shell, ts, tsx],\n})\n```\n\nDo not put server-only imports in this module. The highlighter itself needs none.\n\n## Server path\n\nHighlight before serializing or streaming the code block:\n\n```ts\nconst data = highlighter.renderCodeBlockData({\n  code,\n  lang,\n  title,\n  decorations,\n})\n```\n\nSend or render `data.htmlMarkup`. Keep `data.copyText` for a copy button.\n\n## Hydration\n\nServer-rendered code does not need to be highlighted again. It is already static HTML controlled by CSS.\n\nUse the client highlighter only for code introduced after hydration:\n\n- Client-side route content not included in the initial payload\n- Live Markdown previews\n- Interactive examples that change source\n- User-selected language variants\n\n## Determinism\n\nServer and client output match when all of these match:\n\n- Source string\n- Language registrations and order\n- Language option\n- Decorations and line-number option\n- Package version\n\nThemes do not affect highlighted markup.\n\n## Avoid hydration mismatches\n\n- Export one registry module used by both paths.\n- Do not conditionally register languages with `window` checks.\n- Normalize Markdown fence metadata before rendering on both paths.\n- Do not highlight trimmed code on one path and untrimmed code on the other.\n\n`renderCodeBlockData()` and `renderCodeFence()` trim trailing block whitespace consistently for copy/render workflows. `highlight()` preserves its input exactly.\n\n## Caching\n\nThe highlighter is fast enough for normal docs pages without a cache. For large static builds, cache by package version, language, source, and decoration options if build time becomes material.\n\nDo not cache theme variants separately. They share the same HTML.\n\n## Why no worker?\n\nThe docs-sized path is synchronous and usually much cheaper than worker startup and message serialization. A worker is reasonable only for unusually large interactive inputs, which is outside the primary use case.\n"}
